+"""Attestation provider protocol, trust domain, and L3 publication signatures.
+
+This module implements the protocol frozen by I-08-A (``decision.md`` r3):
+
+* one-shot provider subprocess (request JSON on stdin, response JSON on stdout);
+* exact request/response field sets with a byte-identical echo of
+  ``request_id`` / ``payload_sha256`` / ``domain_separator``;
+* an Ed25519 signature over ``canonical_sha256(payload)`` as 64 ASCII hex chars;
+* a data-file trust domain whose key name is ``public_keys`` (never a code
+  constant), validated as a closed named field set;
+* the single normative error-code table (E01..E32) as the ONLY source of failure
+  codes;
+* the three legacy classes G1 / G2 / G3a / G3b->G4 with a single ``classify()``
+  judgement.
+
+Design rules that must not be relaxed (see ``execution_runs/I-08-A``):
+
+* R-PROV-1: file existence / executability / ".py-ness" is NEVER evidence of
+  signing capability.  Capability means "one successful handshake".
+* R-PROV-2: test keys live in an isolated trust domain only; ``environment``
+  containing ``test`` is rejected on the formal publication path.
+* R-LAYER-2: ``host_signed`` can only be produced by a verified L3 record.
+* R-REPLAY-1: re-verifying the same immutable artifact must always pass, even
+  after ``expires_at``; ``expires_at`` constrains the publish instant only.
+
+OPEN items (NOT decided here, see ``decision.md`` section 8):
+
+* OPEN-D7: the numeric parameters ``W`` (publication window), ``T`` (provider
+  timeout) and ``L`` (provider stdout cap) have no evidentiary basis yet.  They
+  are read from the environment.  When ``T`` or ``L`` is unset the provider call
+  is REFUSED (``provider_call_budget_unspecified``) -- the implementation never
+  substitutes an invented value and never waits without bound.  When ``W`` is
+  unset no upper bound is enforced and ``W_enforced`` is reported as ``false``.
+* OPEN-D1/D2/D3: the authoritative trust root, private-key custody and
+  revocation retroactivity are untouched; a missing trust-domain file stays a
+  legal "zero trusted signers" (fail closed).
+"""
